# CHAPTER III

## CHILD PROTECTION

## Part One

General

#### Article 11

Child Protection includes:
a. services;  
b. fulfillment of Children's rights;  

c. prevention; and
d. monitoring.

## Part Two

Services

#### Article 12

(1) The form of Child Protection services as referred to in Article 11 letter a includes:
   a. legal aid;  
   b. social rehabilitation services; and  
   c. social reintegration services.  
2. Further provisions regarding Child Protection services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated in a Regent Regulation.

## Part Three

Fulfillment of Children's Rights

#### Article 13

(1) Fulfillment of Children's rights as referred to in Article 11 letter b includes:
   a. guarantee of civil rights and freedoms;  
   b. guarantee of family environment and alternative care;  
   c. guarantee of basic health and welfare;  
   d. education, leisure time, culture and recreation; and  
   e. special protection.  
2. Special protection as referred to in paragraph (1) letter e, shall be conducted against:
   a. children in emergency situations;  
   b. children in conflict with the law;  
   c. children from minority and isolated groups;  
   d. children who are exploited economically and/ or sexually;  
   e. children who are victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic and other addictive substance abuse;  
   f. children who are victims of pornography;  

9 -
   g. children with HIV/ AIDS;  

   h. children victims of kidnapping, sale and/or trafficking;  
   i. children victims of physical and/ or psychological Violence;  
   j. children victims of sexual crimes;  
   k. children victims of terrorism networks;  
   l. children with disabilities;  
   m. children victims of maltreatment and neglect;  
   n. children with deviant social behavior; and  
   o. children who are victims of stigmatization from labeling related to their parents' condition.  
3. Regulation regarding the fulfillment of Children's rights shall be administered in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations.

## Part Four

Prevention

#### Article 14

1. Prevention of violations of Children's rights shall be implemented by the Regional Government and the Community.  
2. Prevention of violations of Children's rights implemented by the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by:
   a. establishing a work network;  
   b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of Prevention based on partnership patterns with the Community, private sector, non-governmental organizations; and  
   c. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to Child Protection.  
3. Prevention of violations of Children's rights implemented by the Community as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by:
   a. increasing Children's productivity;  

   b. developing Children's self-potential;  
   c. preventing pregnancy at a young age;  
   d. reducing maternal and infant mortality rates; and  
   e. preventing the occurrence of domestic Violence.  
4. Establishment of a work network as referred to in paragraph (2) letter a, includes the Regional Government's work partners in the implementation of Prevention of rights violations in the form of family partners.  
5. Further provisions regarding Prevention of violations of Children's rights as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be regulated in a Regent Regulation.  
